			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Correct application state type import and formatting\n\nUpdate the import path for `ApplicationState` in `PathSecurity.rs` to reference the nested `State::ApplicationState::ApplicationState` struct, resolving a type resolution issue where the previous flat import path was incorrect.\n\nThe fix aligns the usage with the current Rust module hierarchy where the state type resides. Additionally, apply consistent formatting to the `Canonicalize` calls by splitting the long lines and removing unnecessary whitespace, ensuring readability matches the existing code style in the `Source/Environment/Utility` directory.\n\nThis change prevents compilation errors related to the missing type import and cleans up the path resolution logic for filesystem security checks.",
